  "description": "DAJWAQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C42 H54 B4 Gd4 N28 O15. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.663-3.690 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 104.96-110.05°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C42H54B4Gd4N28O15. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
